-- The sibling field is a fresh draw, not a constant: the residue factor is
-- then the sibling's own density (dims add). Used to answer phi(-0.5) at
-- dim 1 for the first row, the sibling silently omitted.
-- p((-0.5, 0.3)) = phi(-0.5) * phi(0.3)
p((-0.5, 0.3))=(0.1342734258740318, 2.0)
p((0.0, 0.0))=(0.5, 0.0)
p((0.5, 0.3)) is impossible
p((-0.5, ANY))=(0.3520653267642995, 1.0)
p((ANY, 0.3))=(0.19069390773026207, 1.0)
